        "James"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "toc1",
      "content": [
        "James"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "toc2",
      "content": [
        "James"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "toc3",
      "content": [
        "JAS"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "mt1",
      "content": [
        "James"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "chapter",
      "marker": "c",
      "number": "1",
      "sid": "JAS 1"
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "A Greeting from James"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "r",
      "content": [
        "(",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "JUD 1-2",
          "content": [
            "Jude 1:1–2"
          ]
        },
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "1",
          "sid": "JAS 1:1"
        },
        "James, a servant of God and of ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " Lord Jesus Christ,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        "To the twelve tribes of the Dispersion:",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "1:1 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "Literally "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "To the twelve tribes in the Diaspora"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                ". Originally referring to the Jewish people living outside the land of Israel, "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "the Diaspora "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "is applied here to the Jewish believers scattered abroad."
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        "Greetings."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "Rejoicing in Trials"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "r",
      "content": [
        "(",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "PHP 1:12-20",
          "content": [
            "Philippians 1:12–20"
          ]
        },
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "2",
          "sid": "JAS 1:2"
        },
        "Consider ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "it"
          ]
        },
        " pure joy, my brothers, when you encounter trials of many kinds, ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "3",
          "sid": "JAS 1:3"
        },
        "because you know that the testing of your faith develops perseverance. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "4",
          "sid": "JAS 1:4"
        },
        "Allow perseverance to finish ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "its"
          ]
        },
        " work, so that you may be mature and complete, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "not"
          ]
        },
        " lacking ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "anything"
          ]
        },
        "."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "5",
          "sid": "JAS 1:5"
        },
        "Now if any of you lacks wisdom, he should ask God, who gives generously to all without finding fault, and it will be given to him. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "6",
          "sid": "JAS 1:6"
        },
        "But he must ask in faith, without doubting, because he who doubts is like a wave of ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " sea, blown and tossed by the wind. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "7",
          "sid": "JAS 1:7"
        },
        "That man ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "should"
          ]
        },
        " not expect to receive anything from the Lord. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "8",
          "sid": "JAS 1:8"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "He is"
          ]
        },
        " a double-minded man, unstable in all his ways."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "9",
          "sid": "JAS 1:9"
        },
        "The brother in humble circumstances should exult in his high position. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "10",
          "sid": "JAS 1:10"
        },
        "But the ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "one who is"
          ]
        },
        " rich ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "should exult"
          ]
        },
        " in his low position, because he will pass away like a flower of the field. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "11",
          "sid": "JAS 1:11"
        },
        "For the sun rises with scorching heat and withers the plant; its flower falls and ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "its"
          ]
        },
        " beauty is lost. So too, the rich ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "man"
          ]
        },
        " will fade away in the midst of his pursuits."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "12",
          "sid": "JAS 1:12"
        },
        "Blessed ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "is the"
          ]
        },
        " man who perseveres under trial, because when he has stood the test, he will receive the crown of life that ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "God"
          ]
        },
        " has promised to those who love Him."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "Good and Perfect Gifts"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "13",
          "sid": "JAS 1:13"
        },
        "When tempted, no one should say, “God is tempting me.” For God cannot be tempted by evil, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "nor"
          ]
        },
        " does He tempt ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "anyone"
          ]
        },
        ". ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "14",
          "sid": "JAS 1:14"
        },
        "But each one is tempted ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "when"
          ]
        },
        " by ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "his"
          ]
        },
        " own evil desires he is lured away and enticed. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "15",
          "sid": "JAS 1:15"
        },
        "Then ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "after"
          ]
        },
        " desire has conceived, it gives birth to sin; and sin, when it is full-grown, gives birth to death."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "16",
          "sid": "JAS 1:16"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Do"
          ]
        },
        " not be deceived, my beloved brothers. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "17",
          "sid": "JAS 1:17"
        },
        "Every good and perfect gift is from above, coming down from the Father of the heavenly lights, with whom there is no change or shifting shadow.",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "1:17 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "Or "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "no change or shadow of turning."
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "18",
          "sid": "JAS 1:18"
        },
        "He chose to give us birth through ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " word of truth, that we would be a kind of firstfruits of His creation.",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "1:18 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "Or "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "of His creatures."
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "Hearing and Doing"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "19",
          "sid": "JAS 1:19"
        },
        "My beloved brothers, understand this: Everyone should be quick to listen, slow to speak, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " slow to anger, ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "20",
          "sid": "JAS 1:20"
        },
        "for man’s anger ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "does"
          ]
        },
        " not bring about ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " righteousness that God ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "desires"
          ]
        },
        ". ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "21",
          "sid": "JAS 1:21"
        },
        "Therefore, get rid of all moral filth and every expression of evil, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " humbly accept the word planted ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "in you"
          ]
        },
        ", which can save your souls."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "22",
          "sid": "JAS 1:22"
        },
        "Be doers of ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " word, and not hearers only. ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Otherwise,"
          ]
        },
        " you are deceiving yourselves. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "23",
          "sid": "JAS 1:23"
        },
        "For anyone who hears ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " word but does not carry it out is like a man ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "who"
          ]
        },
        " looks at his face in a mirror, ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "24",
          "sid": "JAS 1:24"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " after observing himself goes away and immediately forgets what he ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "looks"
          ]
        },
        " like. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "25",
          "sid": "JAS 1:25"
        },
        "But the ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "one who"
          ]
        },
        " looks intently into ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " perfect law of freedom, and continues to do so — not being a forgetful hearer, but an effective doer — ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "he"
          ]
        },
        " will be blessed in what he does."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "26",
          "sid": "JAS 1:26"
        },
        "If anyone considers himself religious ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and yet"
          ]
        },
        " does not bridle his tongue, he deceives his heart ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and his"
          ]
        },
        " religion ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "is"
          ]
        },
        " worthless. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "27",
          "sid": "JAS 1:27"
        },
        "Pure and undefiled religion before ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "our"
          ]
        },
        " God and Father is this: to care for orphans and widows in their distress, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " to keep oneself from being polluted by the world."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "chapter",
      "marker": "c",
      "number": "2",
      "sid": "JAS 2"
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "A Warning against Favoritism"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "1",
          "sid": "JAS 2:1"
        },
        "My brothers, as you hold out ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "your"
          ]
        },
        " faith in our glorious Lord Jesus Christ, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "do"
          ]
        },
        " not ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "show"
          ]
        },
        " favoritism."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "2",
          "sid": "JAS 2:2"
        },
        "Suppose a man comes into your meeting",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "2:2 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "Greek "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "your synagogue"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "wearing"
          ]
        },
        " a gold ring ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " fine clothes, and a poor ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "man"
          ]
        },
        " in shabby clothes also comes in. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "3",
          "sid": "JAS 2:3"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "If"
          ]
        },
        " you lavish attention on the ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "man"
          ]
        },
        " in fine clothes and say, “Here ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "is"
          ]
        },
        " a seat of honor,” ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "but"
          ]
        },
        " say to the poor ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "man"
          ]
        },
        ", “You must stand” or “Sit at my feet,” ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "4",
          "sid": "JAS 2:4"
        },
        "have you not discriminated among yourselves and become judges ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "with"
          ]
        },
        " evil thoughts?"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "5",
          "sid": "JAS 2:5"
        },
        "Listen, my beloved brothers: ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Has"
          ]
        },
        " not God chosen the poor of this world ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "to be"
          ]
        },
        " rich in faith and to inherit the kingdom He promised those who love Him? ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "6",
          "sid": "JAS 2:6"
        },
        "But you have dishonored the poor. ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Is it"
          ]
        },
        " not the rich who oppress you and drag you into court? ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "7",
          "sid": "JAS 2:7"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Are"
          ]
        },
        " they not the ones who blaspheme the noble name by which you have been called?",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "2:7 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "Or "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "the noble name invoked upon you "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "or "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "the noble name of Him to whom you belong"
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "8",
          "sid": "JAS 2:8"
        },
        "If you really fulfill ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " royal law stated in Scripture, “Love your neighbor as yourself,”",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "2:8 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "ref",
                  "loc": "LEV 19:18",
                  "content": [
                    "Leviticus 19:18"
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        " you are doing well. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "9",
          "sid": "JAS 2:9"
        },
        "But if you show favoritism, you sin ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " are convicted by the law as transgressors."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "10",
          "sid": "JAS 2:10"
        },
        "Whoever keeps the whole law but stumbles at just one ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "point"
          ]
        },
        " is guilty of ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "breaking"
          ]
        },
        " all of it. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "11",
          "sid": "JAS 2:11"
        },
        "For He who said, “Do not commit adultery,”",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "2:11 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "ref",
                  "loc": "EXO 20:14",
                  "content": [
                    "Exodus 20:14"
                  ]
                },
                "; Deuteronomy 5:18"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        " also said, “Do not murder.”",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "2:11 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "ref",
                  "loc": "EXO 20:13",
                  "content": [
                    "Exodus 20:13"
                  ]
                },
                "; Deuteronomy 5:17"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        " If you do not commit adultery, but do commit murder, you have become a lawbreaker."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "12",
          "sid": "JAS 2:12"
        },
        "Speak and act as those who are going to be judged by ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " law that gives freedom. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "13",
          "sid": "JAS 2:13"
        },
        "For judgment without mercy  ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "will be shown to "
          ]
        },
        " anyone who has not been merciful. Mercy triumphs over judgment."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "Faith and Works"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "r",
      "content": [
        "(",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "GAL 3:1-9",
          "content": [
            "Galatians 3:1–9"
          ]
        },
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "14",
          "sid": "JAS 2:14"
        },
        "What good ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "is it"
          ]
        },
        ", my brothers, if someone claims to have faith, but has no deeds? Can such faith save him? ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "15",
          "sid": "JAS 2:15"
        },
        "Suppose a brother or sister is without clothes and daily food. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "16",
          "sid": "JAS 2:16"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "If"
          ]
        },
        " one of you tells him, “Go in peace; stay warm and well fed,” but ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "does"
          ]
        },
        " not provide for ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "his"
          ]
        },
        " physical needs, what good ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "is that "
          ]
        },
        "? ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "17",
          "sid": "JAS 2:17"
        },
        "So too, faith by itself, if it does not result in action,",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "2:17 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "Literally "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "if it does not have works"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        " is dead."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "18",
          "sid": "JAS 2:18"
        },
        "But someone will say, “You have faith and I have deeds.” Show me your faith without deeds, and I will show you ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "my"
          ]
        },
        " faith by my deeds. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "19",
          "sid": "JAS 2:19"
        },
        "You believe that God is one.",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "2:19 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "Or "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "that there is one God"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        " Good for you! Even the demons believe ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "that"
          ]
        },
        " — and shudder."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "20",
          "sid": "JAS 2:20"
        },
        "O foolish man, do you want evidence that faith without deeds is worthless?",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "2:20 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "BYZ and TR "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "dead"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "21",
          "sid": "JAS 2:21"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Was"
          ]
        },
        " not our father Abraham justified by what he did when he offered his son Isaac on the altar? ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "22",
          "sid": "JAS 2:22"
        },
        "You see that ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "his"
          ]
        },
        " faith was working with his actions, and ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "his"
          ]
        },
        " faith was perfected by what he did. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "23",
          "sid": "JAS 2:23"
        },
        "And the Scripture was fulfilled that says, “Abraham believed God, and it was credited to him as righteousness,”",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "2:23 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "ref",
                  "loc": "GEN 15:6",
                  "content": [
                    "Genesis 15:6"
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        " and he was called a friend of God.",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "2:23 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "See ",
                {
                  "type": "ref",
                  "loc": "ISA 41:8",
                  "content": [
                    "Isaiah 41:8"
                  ]
                },
                "."
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "24",
          "sid": "JAS 2:24"
        },
        "As you can see, a man is justified by ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "his"
          ]
        },
        " deeds and not by faith alone."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "25",
          "sid": "JAS 2:25"
        },
        "In the same way, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "was"
          ]
        },
        " not even Rahab the prostitute justified by her actions when she welcomed the spies",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "2:25 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "Literally "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "messengers"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        " and sent ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "them"
          ]
        },
        " off on another route? ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "26",
          "sid": "JAS 2:26"
        },
        "As the body without ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " spirit is dead, so faith without deeds is dead."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "chapter",
      "marker": "c",
      "number": "3",
      "sid": "JAS 3"
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "Taming the Tongue"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "r",
      "content": [
        "(",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "PSA 64:1-10",
          "content": [
            "Psalm 64:1–10"
          ]
        },
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "1",
          "sid": "JAS 3:1"
        },
        "Not many ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "of you"
          ]
        },
        " should become teachers, my brothers, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "because"
          ]
        },
        " you know that we ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "who teach "
          ]
        },
        " will be judged more strictly. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "2",
          "sid": "JAS 3:2"
        },
        "We all stumble in many ways. If anyone ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "is"
          ]
        },
        " never at fault in what he says, he ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "is"
          ]
        },
        " a perfect man, able to control ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "his"
          ]
        },
        " whole body."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "3",
          "sid": "JAS 3:3"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "When"
          ]
        },
        " we put bits into the mouths of horses to make them obey us, we can guide the whole animal. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "4",
          "sid": "JAS 3:4"
        },
        "Consider ships as well. Although they are so large and are driven by strong winds, they are steered by a very small rudder wherever the pilot is inclined."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "5",
          "sid": "JAS 3:5"
        },
        "In the same way, the tongue is a small part of the body, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "but"
          ]
        },
        " it boasts of great things. Consider how small a spark sets a great forest ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "ablaze"
          ]
        },
        ". ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "6",
          "sid": "JAS 3:6"
        },
        "The tongue also ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "is"
          ]
        },
        " a fire, a world of wickedness among the parts of the ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "body"
          ]
        },
        ". It pollutes the whole person, sets the course of his life ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "on fire"
          ]
        },
        ", and is itself set on fire by hell.",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "3:6 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "Greek "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "Gehenna"
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "7",
          "sid": "JAS 3:7"
        },
        "All kinds of animals, birds, reptiles, and creatures of the sea are being tamed and have been tamed by man, ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "8",
          "sid": "JAS 3:8"
        },
        "but no man can tame the tongue. ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "It is"
          ]
        },
        " a restless evil, full of deadly poison."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "9",
          "sid": "JAS 3:9"
        },
        "With ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the tongue"
          ]
        },
        " we bless our Lord and Father, and with it we curse men, who have been made in God’s likeness. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "10",
          "sid": "JAS 3:10"
        },
        "Out of the same mouth come blessing and cursing. My brothers, this should not be! ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "11",
          "sid": "JAS 3:11"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Can"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "both"
          ]
        },
        " fresh ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "water"
          ]
        },
        " and salt ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "water"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "3:11 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "Literally "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "Can both fresh and bitter"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        " flow from the same spring? ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "12",
          "sid": "JAS 3:12"
        },
        "My brothers, can a fig tree grow olives, or a grapevine ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "bear"
          ]
        },
        " figs? Neither ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "can"
          ]
        },
        " a salt ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "spring"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "3:12 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "Literally "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "Neither can salt"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        " produce fresh water."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "The Wisdom from Above"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "13",
          "sid": "JAS 3:13"
        },
        "Who ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "is"
          ]
        },
        " wise and understanding among you? Let him show it by ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "his"
          ]
        },
        " good conduct, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "by"
          ]
        },
        " deeds ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "done"
          ]
        },
        " in ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " humility that comes from wisdom. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "14",
          "sid": "JAS 3:14"
        },
        "But if you ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "harbor"
          ]
        },
        " bitter jealousy and selfish ambition in your hearts, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "do"
          ]
        },
        " not boast ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "in it"
          ]
        },
        " or deny the truth. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "15",
          "sid": "JAS 3:15"
        },
        "Such wisdom ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "does"
          ]
        },
        " not come from above, but ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "is"
          ]
        },
        " earthly, unspiritual, demonic. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "16",
          "sid": "JAS 3:16"
        },
        "For where jealousy and selfish ambition ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "exist"
          ]
        },
        ", there ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "will be "
          ]
        },
        " disorder and every evil practice."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "17",
          "sid": "JAS 3:17"
        },
        "But ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " wisdom from above is first ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "of all"
          ]
        },
        " pure, then peace-loving, gentle, accommodating, full of mercy and good fruit, impartial, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " sincere. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "18",
          "sid": "JAS 3:18"
        },
        "Peacemakers ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "who"
          ]
        },
        " sow in peace ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "reap "
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " fruit of righteousness.",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "3:18 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "Literally "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "But the fruit of righteousness is sown in peace by those making peace."
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "chapter",
      "marker": "c",
      "number": "4",
      "sid": "JAS 4"
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "A Warning against Pride"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "1",
          "sid": "JAS 4:1"
        },
        "What ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "causes"
          ]
        },
        " conflicts and quarrels among you? Don’t ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "they"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "come"
          ]
        },
        " from ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " passions at war within you?",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "4:1 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "Literally "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "passions warring among your members?"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "2",
          "sid": "JAS 4:2"
        },
        "You crave ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "what"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "you do"
          ]
        },
        " not have; you kill and covet, but are unable to obtain ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "it"
          ]
        },
        ". You quarrel and fight. You do not have, because you ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "do"
          ]
        },
        " not ask. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "3",
          "sid": "JAS 4:3"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "And when"
          ]
        },
        " you do ask, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "you do"
          ]
        },
        " not receive, because you ask with wrong motives, that you may squander ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "it"
          ]
        },
        " on your pleasures."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "4",
          "sid": "JAS 4:4"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "You"
          ]
        },
        " adulteresses!",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "4:4 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "See ",
                {
                  "type": "ref",
                  "loc": "HOS 3:1",
                  "content": [
                    "Hosea 3:1"
                  ]
                },
                "."
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        " Do you not know that friendship with the world is hostility ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "toward"
          ]
        },
        " God? Therefore, whoever chooses to be a friend of the world renders himself",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "4:4 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "Or "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "is appointed"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        " an enemy of God. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "5",
          "sid": "JAS 4:5"
        },
        "Or do you think the Scripture says without reason ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "that"
          ]
        },
        " the Spirit",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "4:5 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "Or "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "the spirit"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        " He caused to dwell in us yearns with envy? ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "6",
          "sid": "JAS 4:6"
        },
        "But He gives ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "us"
          ]
        },
        " more grace. This is why it says:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "b"
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        "“God opposes ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " proud,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        "but gives grace to ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " humble.”",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "4:6 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "ref",
                  "loc": "PRO 3:34",
                  "content": [
                    "Proverbs 3:34"
                  ]
                },
                " (see also LXX)"
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "Drawing Near to God"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "7",
          "sid": "JAS 4:7"
        },
        "Submit yourselves, then, to God. Resist the devil, and he will flee from you. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "8",
          "sid": "JAS 4:8"
        },
        "Draw near to God, and He will draw near to you. Cleanse ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "your"
          ]
        },
        " hands, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "you"
          ]
        },
        " sinners, and purify ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "your"
          ]
        },
        " hearts, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "you"
          ]
        },
        " double-minded. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "9",
          "sid": "JAS 4:9"
        },
        "Grieve, mourn, and weep. Turn your laughter to mourning, and ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "your"
          ]
        },
        " joy to gloom. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "10",
          "sid": "JAS 4:10"
        },
        "Humble yourselves before ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " Lord, and He will exalt you."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "11",
          "sid": "JAS 4:11"
        },
        "Brothers, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "do"
          ]
        },
        " not slander one another. Anyone who speaks against ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "his"
          ]
        },
        " brother or judges ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "him"
          ]
        },
        " speaks against ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " law and judges ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "it"
          ]
        },
        ". And if you judge ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " law, you are not a practitioner of ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " law, but a judge ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "of it"
          ]
        },
        ". ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "12",
          "sid": "JAS 4:12"
        },
        "There is only one Lawgiver and Judge, the ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "One who"
          ]
        },
        " is able to save and destroy. But who are you to judge ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "your"
          ]
        },
        " neighbor?"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "Do Not Boast about Tomorrow"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "r",
      "content": [
        "(",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "PRO 27:1",
          "content": [
            "Proverbs 27:1"
          ]
        },
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "13",
          "sid": "JAS 4:13"
        },
        "Come now, you who say, “Today or tomorrow we will go to this or that city, spend a year there, carry on business, and make a profit.” ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "14",
          "sid": "JAS 4:14"
        },
        "You do not even know what ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "will happen"
          ]
        },
        " tomorrow! What ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "is"
          ]
        },
        " your life? You are a mist that appears for a little ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "while"
          ]
        },
        " and then vanishes."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "15",
          "sid": "JAS 4:15"
        },
        "Instead, you ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "ought"
          ]
        },
        " to say, “If the Lord is willing, we will live and do this or that.” ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "16",
          "sid": "JAS 4:16"
        },
        "As it is, you boast in your proud intentions. All such boasting is evil. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "17",
          "sid": "JAS 4:17"
        },
        "Anyone, then, who knows ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " right thing to do, yet fails to do ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "it"
          ]
        },
        ", is guilty of sin."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "chapter",
      "marker": "c",
      "number": "5",
      "sid": "JAS 5"
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "A Warning to the Rich"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "r",
      "content": [
        "(",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "PRO 23:1-5",
          "content": [
            "Proverbs 23:1–5"
          ]
        },
        "; ",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "1TI 6:17-19",
          "content": [
            "1 Timothy 6:17–19"
          ]
        },
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "1",
          "sid": "JAS 5:1"
        },
        "Come now, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "you who are"
          ]
        },
        " rich, weep ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " wail over the misery to come upon you. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "2",
          "sid": "JAS 5:2"
        },
        "Your riches have rotted and moths have eaten your clothes. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "3",
          "sid": "JAS 5:3"
        },
        "Your gold and silver are corroded. Their corrosion will testify against you and consume your flesh like fire."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        "You have hoarded treasure in ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " last days. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "4",
          "sid": "JAS 5:4"
        },
        "Look, the wages you withheld from the workmen who mowed your fields are crying out against you. The cries of the harvesters have reached the ears of ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " Lord of Hosts."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "5",
          "sid": "JAS 5:5"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "You have lived"
          ]
        },
        " on earth in luxury and self-indulgence. You have fattened your hearts in ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " day of slaughter. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "6",
          "sid": "JAS 5:6"
        },
        "You have condemned ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " murdered the righteous, who did not resist you."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "Patience in Suffering"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "r",
      "content": [
        "(",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "JOB 1:1-5",
          "content": [
            "Job 1:1–5"
          ]
        },
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "7",
          "sid": "JAS 5:7"
        },
        "Be patient, then, brothers, until the Lord’s coming. See how the farmer awaits the precious fruit of the soil — how patient he is for ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the fall"
          ]
        },
        " and ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "spring rains"
          ]
        },
        ".",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "5:7 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "Literally "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "for it until it receives the early and the late"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "8",
          "sid": "JAS 5:8"
        },
        "You, too, be patient ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " strengthen your hearts, because the Lord’s coming is near. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "9",
          "sid": "JAS 5:9"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Do"
          ]
        },
        " not complain about one another, brothers, so that you will not be judged. Look, the Judge is standing at the door!"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "10",
          "sid": "JAS 5:10"
        },
        "Brothers, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "as"
          ]
        },
        " an example of patience in affliction, take the prophets who spoke in the name of ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " Lord. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "11",
          "sid": "JAS 5:11"
        },
        "See how blessed we consider those who have persevered. You have heard of Job’s perseverance and have seen the outcome from ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " Lord. The Lord is full of compassion and mercy."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "12",
          "sid": "JAS 5:12"
        },
        "Above all, my brothers, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "do"
          ]
        },
        " not swear, not ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "by"
          ]
        },
        " heaven ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "or"
          ]
        },
        " earth ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "or by"
          ]
        },
        " any other oath. Simply ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "let"
          ]
        },
        " your “Yes” be yes, and ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "your"
          ]
        },
        " “No,” no, so that you will not fall under judgment."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "The Prayer of Faith"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "13",
          "sid": "JAS 5:13"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Is"
          ]
        },
        " any one of you suffering? He should pray. ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Is"
          ]
        },
        " anyone cheerful? He should sing praises. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "14",
          "sid": "JAS 5:14"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Is"
          ]
        },
        " any one of you sick? He should call the elders of the church to pray over him and anoint him with oil in the name of the Lord. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "15",
          "sid": "JAS 5:15"
        },
        "And the prayer offered in faith will restore the one who is sick. The Lord will raise him up. If he has sinned, he will be forgiven."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "16",
          "sid": "JAS 5:16"
        },
        "Therefore confess ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "your"
          ]
        },
        " sins to each other and pray for each other so that you may be healed. ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "The"
          ]
        },
        " prayer of a righteous ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "man"
          ]
        },
        " has great power to prevail. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "17",
          "sid": "JAS 5:17"
        },
        "Elijah was a man just like us. He prayed earnestly ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "that it would"
          ]
        },
        " not rain, and it did not rain on the land for three and ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "a half"
          ]
        },
        " years. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "18",
          "sid": "JAS 5:18"
        },
        "Again he prayed, and the heavens gave rain, and the earth yielded its crops."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "Restoring a Sinner"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "19",
          "sid": "JAS 5:19"
        },
        "My brothers, if one of you should wander from the truth and someone should bring him back, ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "20",
          "sid": "JAS 5:20"
        },
        "consider this: Whoever turns a sinner from ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " error of his way will save his soul from death and cover over a multitude of sins."
      ]
    }
  ]
}